    {
      "id": "GPM-01",
      "title": "An index makes the logarithmic metric independent of the chosen section",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-period-line",
      "statement": "For the τ-coordinate module in a compatible number field M, Ω̄τ = (2 log [ℓτ:𝒪_M s] − Σρ log(π|ρ(s)|²/Aρ))/[M:ℚ]. When ℓτ=𝒪_M a, this is the mean of −log(π|ρ(a)|²/Aρ).",
      "hypotheses": "Nonzero curve ideal prime to 2d, twelfth root of its elliptic-lattice discriminant, all torus embeddings and g₂,g₃ contained in M; s is a nonzero element of ℓτ. The generator form uses a spanning generator.",
