    {
      "id": "GPM-02",
      "title": "The quadratic CM period and the correction from the relative different",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-period-scalar",
      "statement": "For every compatible M and τ, Ω̄τ equals the mean of log(Aρ/π) minus (2/[E:ℚ])log b, where b is the absolute norm of the product of the host fractional ideal and the relative different. This equals γ + log(2π/rd E) − Re(L′(1,χ)/L(1,χ)).",
      "hypotheses": "Host conditions of D7 for the imaginary quadratic field K₀ of discriminant −d, its host extension E and relative half-different data; admissible curve ideal, discriminant twelfth root and compatible number field.",
